     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju measured a pencil as 12 cm 5 mm.\n\"That is 12.5 cm,\" said his teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "tenth",
     "hundredth",
     "decimal"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "When whole units are too big we use smaller units. One tenth is one of ten equal parts, written 0.1. One hundredth is one of a hundred equal parts, written 0.01.\nUnits give examples: 1 cm is 0.01 m, 1 mm is 0.1 cm and 1 paisa is 0.01 rupee. So 12 cm 5 mm is 12.5 cm.\nIn 3.47, the 4 is in the tenths place and the 7 is in the hundredths place."
    }
